Delvers Core adds Lowell, Liana and Kragas as recruits in Custom Expedition and in the guild, for no more than 500 gold each, and Apocalypse, a new difficulty above Downfall. It is also the base for character packs such as [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dungeonsettlers/mods/13]Delvers Frieren[/url], and it protects modded campaigns: if loading goes wrong, Core blocks saving and tells you.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]

[b]Apocalypse difficulty.[/b] One step above Downfall, separately for combat and management. You can choose it for a new campaign once Downfall is unlocked. In combat, enemies attack at once and the pause key only slows time for a few seconds. In management, merchants offer fewer goods. Without Core, such a campaign loads as Downfall.

[b]Forest bandits.[/b] A faction of their own in combat Apocalypse, with their own group control. Watch your step in the forest.

[b]Bleeding and first aid.[/b] In combat Apocalypse, bleeding no longer stops on its own and gets worse in stages. Bandages, the aid kit, the portal or a revive stop it. Characters can treat each other, and bandages can be bought or made.

[b]Revival.[/b] With the revive scroll, a living character brings a fallen party member back after a short wait. How often depends on the combat difficulty, and the revived character stays weakened for a while.

[b]Enemy abilities.[/b] In combat Apocalypse, some enemies cause bleeding, silence or sleep.

[b]Gear on the fallen.[/b] Fallen characters keep their equipment. Alt and right click on a body offers "Strip Equipment". Core asks before a dressed body is buried.

[b]Shield band.[/b] A band over the health bar shows a character's shield.

[b]Tactical formation (experimental).[/b] Each character gets a place in a lineup that follows a leader through the dungeon, plus places for skills the character casts first.

[b]Group AI (experimental).[/b] Optional target choice, spacing, dodging and bandages for characters left on auto attack; up to Hard, off by default.

[b]Delvers menu.[/b] The last tab in the game's options holds every switch of Core, from the title menu. You can turn the three founders off one by one, and switch each Apocalypse rule on for other difficulties too.

[b]Guide.[/b] At the bottom of the game's guide, a Delvers section explains the rules and switches, with its own pictures.

[size=4][b]Requirements and compatibility[/b][/size]

Windows x64, Dungeon Settlers DS_B.0.4.29 (Steam build 25846389) and BepInEx 6 for Unity IL2CPP x64, tested with 6.0.0-be.788. Delvers runs on BepInEx only.

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dungeonsettlers/mods/13]Delvers Frieren[/url] 0.5.0 works with Core 0.5.0 and 0.5.1. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/dungeonsettlers/mods/5]Extended Hotbar[/url] 1.0.1 to 1.0.3 is recognized as compatible.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Back up your saves first. Then extract the ZIP into the Dungeon Settlers game folder; it already contains the required folders. To update, extract the new ZIP over the old files.

Moving from MelonLoader: remove the old Core DLLs from Mods/ and UserLibs/ first.

[size=4][b]New in 0.5.1[/b][/size]

Extended Hotbar 1.0.3 is recognized as compatible.

Fixed: Delvers bandages on the extra slots of Extended Hotbar now stay there after loading.

[size=4][b]Reporting problems[/b][/size]

Please include your game build, BepInEx version and the log.

